-- =============================================================================
-- BASELINE 05 — Scheduled jobs (pg_cron)  ** REFERENCE ONLY — DO NOT AUTO-APPLY **
-- =============================================================================
-- Captured from cron.job on the live project (ytnnsykbgohiscfgomfe), 2026-08-01.
-- Deliberately named *.reference so the Supabase CLI does NOT pick it up as a
-- migration. Running it as-is would fail or double-schedule.
--
-- Two reasons it is reference-only:
--   1. Bearer tokens are REDACTED. Jobs 14-50 embed a JWT directly in the cron
--      command. Those values must never be committed, so they are stubbed as
--      <REDACTED_JWT>. Recreating a job requires substituting the real key.
--   2. cron.schedule() with an existing jobname updates it, but the URLs here are
--      hardcoded to the production project ref and would be wrong elsewhere.
--
-- NOTE the two patterns in use. Jobs 54 and 55 are the good one: they read
-- credentials at runtime via get_app_setting() from the app_settings table
-- instead of embedding a key in the job definition. Every job recreated during
-- the v2 rewrite should follow that pattern so this file can become a real,
-- committable migration with no secrets in it.
--
-- 19 active jobs. Many of these disappear in v2 — see docs/V2_PLAN.md section 9
-- (kill list). Specifically: schedule-daily-prompts, send-daily-notifications,
-- all birthday-card jobs, all custom-question jobs, and the interest/discovery
-- personalization jobs.
-- =============================================================================

-- job 14  (schedule-daily-prompts)          -- v2: DELETE
SELECT cron.schedule('schedule-daily-prompts', '1 0 * * *', $cron$
  SELECT
    net.http_post(
      url:='https://ytnnsykbgohiscfgomfe.supabase.co/functions/v1/schedule-daily-prompts',
      headers:='{"Content-Type": "application/json", "Authorization": "Bearer <REDACTED_JWT>"}'::jsonb
    ) AS request_id;
  $cron$);

